# Chapter-36 observable-inference slice (slice 41).
#
# A pipeline slice. Its inputs are the slice-39 stream, slice 39's and
# slice 40's printed environment rows, and the ffi-builtin table, and it
# ports the next step of `lower/lower` after the F38 check, the first
# observable-inference passes.
#
#   1. infer-observables-in-record-env with defer? true. Each record's
#      observables are typed against the record env as build-record-env
#      left it (no record has an observable index yet), bare field idents
#      read as `self.<field>` unless a param shadows them
#      (rewrite-self-field-refs).
#   2. the atom pass of finalize-atom-env-inference,
#      infer-observables-in-atom-env with defer? true. Observables are
#      typed in declaration order, each typed one joins the atom's
#      self-fields and (when its type is known) its observable index, so
#      a later observable reads an earlier one.
#   3. (chapter 37) infer-streams-in-atom-env, the second step of
#      finalize-atom-env-inference, with the same typer. Per atom the
#      ctor locals, then per transition its context (ctor locals and self
#      for an on-enter arm of the initial phase, self alone for another
#      on-enter arm, self and the payload locals for a receive arm), the
#      alias heads of its `then` clauses folded in where they type, and
#      every untargeted emit in rendering order. An arg whose typing
#      throws or gives nil drops its site. The sites are reduced by
#      stream, the first one's types giving the C types and every later
#      one checked key by key. The context reads every atom's observable
#      index and its own observables as self-fields, as the first atom
#      pass left them.
#
# (chapter 38) The `round2` mode is slice 43, the second inference round.
# It runs the three passes above again first (their types are recomputed
# in process, printed rows drop the size_t mark), then in lower's order
#
#   4. infer-protocol-defaults. Each default of every protocol row whose
#      `:cxc-return-ty` is nil is typed with no locals and no self-fields,
#      against the first-round envs, under the full ctx. The ctx carries
#      the module map, so enum-case access (`E.c`), enum payload calls
#      (`E.c(...)`), and `R.from(...)` resolve through resolve-decl-lookup
#      (the refs row of the protocol's piece, else the
#      ensure-references-enriched fallback, then the module map row). A
#      `:not-yet-implemented` error leaves the default untyped, any other
#      error propagates, and a type names its return through
#      type-kw->cxc-name-str.
#   5. infer-observables-in-record-env and infer-observables-in-atom-env
#      with defer? false over the env with slice 42's containers. The
#      record pass reads the first round's record and atom indices, the
#      atom pass the second-round record index, the first-round peer
#      indices, and its own threaded index. Container method lookup reads
#      the slice-42 rows (`:cxc-return-ty`, `:return-optional?`, the
#      `count` observable, the `min_by`, `max_by`, and `first` list
#      sugars), and a missing method on an atom now names the sorted
#      available ones. Every container adds `(obs <class> count :int nil)`.
#   6. infer-streams-in-atom-env again over the second-round indices.
#      Every List container adds its fan-in rows to the section.
#
# Per observable, the param locals (bare primitives lift to Optional), a
# declared `:- T` (base-type-name, cxc-type->type-kw, Optional for a bare
# primitive), else try-infer-observation-body on its expression, then
# type-kw->c-type. try-infer-observation-body swallows the three deferred
# user errors (a method or observable missing on an atom, a field or
# method missing on a `_Cxc_ListOf`/`MapOf`/`SetOf` container, a
# self-observation not typed yet), which leave the type nil.
#
# The expression typer (infer-type with infer-binop-type,
# infer-call-type, infer-method-call-type, field-type-for-owner, and
# foreign-type-node->tk) runs on a frame stack over the arena. A frame
# holds the node, its stage, two registers, and the context it replaced.
# The context is the locals table, the self-fields owner and kind (`R` a
# record pass, `A` an atom pass, `P` a peer atom whose untyped
# observable is typed on the fly by field-type-for-owner), and the
# record rewrite is on only in `R`. The inference context carries no
# module map, so enum-case access, enum payload calls, and
# `Record.from(...)` never match here, and no named-tuple env, so a
# named-tuple field read raises.
#
# argv.
#
#   <check> <stream> <envs> <ffi>
#       <check> is `lower` or `envs`, <stream> the slice-39 stream, <envs>
#       slice 39's `(decl ...)`, `(enum ...)`, `(keep ...)`, and
#       `(atom ...)` rows followed by slice 40's `(record ...)` rows, any
#       `error|` line passing through, and <ffi> the ffi-builtin table
#       (`oracle/lower_observables_tables.clj`).
#   round2 <stream> <envs> <ffi> <post> <index> <refs>
#       <envs> also holds slice 39's `(module ...)` and `(protocol ...)`
#       rows. <post> is slice 42's envs output on the first-round rows,
#       its companions and containers, or an error. A lower row puts the
#       parity or collect-shapes error of slice 40's envs run there
#       instead when the companion demand passed. <index> is the prelude
#       name index and <refs> the per-piece refs rows of slice 39.
#
# Output.
#
#   (record-obs <n>)  then (obs <record> <name> <type-kw>|nil "<c-type>"|nil)
#   (atom-obs <n>)    then (obs <atom> <name> <type-kw>|nil "<c-type>"|nil)
#   (stream-payloads <n>)  then (spi <atom> <stream> (<key> <type-kw> "<c-type>")*)
#       Rows sorted. <type-kw> is Clojure's pr-str of the type keyword.
#   round2 prints (protocol-defaults <n>) with sorted
#       (pdefault <protocol> <name> <ret>|nil) rows, then the three
#       sections above for the second round.
#
# A throw in the record pass prints `error|<message>` alone, a throw in
# the atom pass prints the record section first, and a throw in the
# stream pass prints both observable sections first. In round2 a throw
# in the first round, the demand, the parity check, or the protocol
# defaults prints alone, and a later one follows the sections before it.
#
# Type keywords are carried as their pr-str text. SizeT and SsizeT keep
# the C type their metadata carries as a `~size_t` or `~ssize_t` mark
# that printing drops. An error is `!U:` (fail-user!), `!N:` (fail-nyi!),
# or `!C:` (fail-compile!) and the message.
#
# Scope notes. Clojure walks both envs as hash maps, the port takes the
# rows' sorted order, which agrees whenever one observable fails. `Ptr of
# T` in a foreign signature, a successful `stackalloc`, a named tuple in
# a declared return type, a let annotation, or a param, and a peer
# observable chain deeper than 60 frames print the port-only message
# `port: out of scope`, which no corpus row reaches. Protocols are
# typed in name order where Clojure takes the protocol env's hash order,
# which agrees whenever one default fails. The stream pass
# takes emits in rendering order, which is postwalk order unless an
# untargeted emit nests inside another's args, and builds every context
# of an atom before its reduce, which is what Clojure's chunked lazy
# sequence does for up to 32 transitions.

def SNode:
    pre:    Int!
    kind:   Int!
    start:  Int!
    stop:   Int!
    depth:  Int!
    size:   Int!
    parent: Int!

def Frame:
    n:  Int!
    st: Int!
    a:  String!
    b:  Int!
    c:  String!

def main:
    use args:    Args
    use console: Console
    use fs:      FileSystem

    mode:     String! = ""
    src:      String! = ""
    envt:     String! = ""
    ffit:     String! = ""
    out:      String! = ""
    # Reader state.
    rp:       Int!    = 0
    rmode:    Int!    = 0
    rnest:    Int!    = 0
    tstart:   Int!    = 0
    sp:       Int!    = 0
    ncount:   Int!    = 0
    rstack:   List of SNode = []
    nodes:    List of SNode = []
    # Prep.
    gi:       Int!    = 0
    pj:       Int!    = 0
    pe:       Int!    = 0
    pown:     String! = ""
    ftab:     String! = "\n"
    dtab:     String! = "\n"
    otab:     String! = "\n"
    mtab:     String! = "\n"
    recl:     List of String = []
    atl:      List of String = []
    # The two passes.
    pass:     String! = "R"
    pk:       Int!    = 0
    owner:    String! = ""
    oi:       Int!    = 0
    oe:       Int!    = 0
    qk:       Int!    = 0
    otk:      String! = ""
    rotab:    String! = "\n"
    known:    String! = "\n"
    oidx:     String! = "\n"
    rhint:    String! = "\n"
    orows:    List of String = []
    rsec:     String! = ""
    # The stream pass.
    aobs:     String! = "\n"
    cloc:     String! = "\n"
    tloc:     String! = "\n"
    tinit:    String! = ""
    sacc:     String! = ""
    sprev:    String! = ""
    srow:     String! = ""
    sites:    List of String = []
    stab:     String! = "\n"
    sret:     String! = "o"
    # The second round (slice 43).
    rnd:      Int!    = 1
    rotab2:   String! = "\n"
    aobs2:    String! = "\n"
    postt:    String! = ""
    pidxt:    String! = ""
    rsrc:     String! = ""
    pcn:      Int!    = 0
    pc_cur:   Int!    = 0
    cur_mod:  String! = "main"
    dmain:    String! = "\n"
    prl:      List of Int! = []
    ctab:     String! = "\n"
    cobs:     List of String = []
    cspi:     List of String = []
    ferr:     String! = ""
    fpre:     String! = ""
    hx_t:     String! = ""
    # The typer.
    fr:       List of Frame = []
    fd:       Int!    = 0
    cur:      Int!    = 0
    val:      String! = ""
    terr:     String! = ""
    sfk:      String! = "R"
    sfo:      String! = ""
    loc:      String! = "\n"
    pnames:   String! = "\n"
    nac:      Int!    = -1
    aci:      Int!    = 0
    tfs:      String! = ""
    tfp:      Int!    = 0
    tfd:      Int!    = 0
    # Sorting.
    rows:     List of String = []
    sort_ret: String! = ""
    sort_i:   Int!    = 0
    scan_best: String! = ""
    scan_has: Bool!   = false
    sorted:   String! = ""
    nsorted:  Int!    = 0
    tktab:    String! = "\nInt\t:int\nInt8\t[:int 8]\nInt16\t[:int 16]\nInt32\t[:int 32]\nInt64\t[:int 64]\nUInt8\t[:uint 8]\nUInt16\t[:uint 16]\nUInt32\t[:uint 32]\nUInt64\t[:uint 64]\nFloat\t[:float 32]\nDouble\t:float\nString\t:string\nBool\t:bool\nUnit\t:unit\nNever\t:never\nAny\t:any\nBytes\t:bytes\nBlock\t:block\nByte\t[:uint 8]\nSizeT\t[:uint 64]~size_t\nSsizeT\t[:int 64]~ssize_t\nCString\t[:cstring]\n"

    # Reader observations (slice 37).
    r_end    :- rp >= src.length()
    rc       :- ||: r_end : -1 ||: else : src.code_at(rp)
    r_sp     :- rc == 32 or rc == 10 or rc == 9 or rc == 13
    r_open   :- rc == 40
    r_close  :- rc == 41
    r_quote  :- rc == 34
    r_bs     :- rc == 92
    r_plain  :- not r_end and not r_sp and not r_open and not r_close
    rtop     :- rstack.at((sp - 1).max(0)) ?? SNode(pre: -1, kind: 0, start: 0, stop: 0, depth: -1, size: 0, parent: -1)
    r_parent :- ||: sp == 0 : -1 ||: else : rtop.pre
    a_stop   :- r_end or r_sp or (r_close and rnest == 0)

    # Arena accessors.
    nn :- nodes.count()
    sx(i: Int!) :- SNode
        nodes.at(i.max(0)) ?? SNode(pre: -1, kind: -1, start: 0, stop: 0, depth: -1, size: 1, parent: -1)
    sx_text(i: Int!) :- String!
        ||: i < 0 or i >= nn : "" ||: else : src.substring(self.sx(i).start.max(0).min(src.length()), (self.sx(i).stop - self.sx(i).start).max(0).min(src.length()))
    sx_next(i: Int!) :- Int!
        i + self.sx(i).size.max(1)
    sx_head(i: Int!) :- String!
        ||: self.sx(i).kind == 0 and self.sx(i).size > 1 : self.sx_text(i + 1) ||: else : ""
    sx_end(i: Int!) :- Int!
        i + self.sx(i).size
    line_at(t: String!, k: Int!) :- String!
        ||: t.substring(k, t.length() - k).index_of("\n") < 0 : t.substring(k, t.length() - k) ||: else : t.substring(k, t.substring(k, t.length() - k).index_of("\n").max(0))
    cut(t: String!, k: Int!) :- String!
        t.substring(k.max(0).min(t.length()), t.length() - k.max(0).min(t.length()))
    ival(t: String!) :- Int!
        t.to_int_or(0)

    # Tables. `look(tab, key)` is the rest of the `\n<key>\t...` line.
    look(tab: String!, key: String!) :- String!
        ||: tab.index_of(("\n" + key) + "\t") < 0 : "" ||: else : self.line_at(tab, (tab.index_of(("\n" + key) + "\t") + key.length() + 2).max(0).min(tab.length()))
    has_key(tab: String!, key: String!) :- Bool!
        tab.contains(("\n" + key) + "\t")
    put_last(tab: String!, key: String!, v: String!) :- String!
        ||: self.has_key(tab, key) : tab.replace((("\n" + key) + ("\t" + self.look(tab, key))) + "\n", (("\n" + key) + ("\t" + v)) + "\n") ||: else : tab + ((key + "\t") + (v + "\n"))
    put_first(tab: String!, key: String!, v: String!) :- String!
        ||: self.has_key(tab, key) : tab ||: else : tab + ((key + "\t") + (v + "\n"))
    tab_cut(r: String!) :- Int!
        ||: r.index_of("\t") < 0 : r.length() ||: else : r.index_of("\t")
    f_first(r: String!) :- String!
        r.substring(0, self.tab_cut(r))
    f_rest(r: String!) :- String!
        r.substring((self.tab_cut(r) + 1).min(r.length()), (r.length() - self.tab_cut(r) - 1).max(0))
    in_set(st: String!, x: String!) :- Bool!
        st.contains(("\n" + x) + "\n")
    soh :- (1).to_char_string()

    # The Clojure node keyword of an expression rendering.
    kw_of(h: String!) :- String!
        ||: h == "int" : ":lit-int" ||: h == "float" : ":lit-float" ||: h == "string" : ":lit-string" ||: h == "char" : ":lit-char" ||: h == "bool" : ":lit-bool" ||: h == "nil" : ":lit-nil" ||: h == "multi-arm" : ":multi-arm-dispatch" ||: h == "do" : ":do-block-expr" ||: h == "variant" : ":variant-pattern" ||: h.starts_with("?") : ":" + h.substring(1, (h.length() - 1).max(0)) ||: else : ":" + h
    kw(i: Int!) :- String!
        ||: self.sx(i).kind == 1 and self.sx_text(i) == "else" : ":else-marker" ||: else : self.kw_of(self.sx_head(i))

    # The env row reader.
    env_err  :- envt.contains("\nerror|")
    env_errl :- self.line_at(envt, (envt.index_of("\nerror|") + 1).max(0))
    akey(x: String!) :- Bool!
        envt.contains(("\n(keep " + x) + ")\n") or envt.contains(("\n(keep " + x) + " runtime-provided)\n")
    is_rec(x: String!) :- Bool!
        envt.contains(("\n(record " + x) + " ")
    env_enum(x: String!) :- Bool!
        envt.contains(("\n(enum " + x) + " ")
    env_has_decl(x: String!) :- Bool!
        envt.contains(("\n(decl " + x) + " ")
    env_decl(x: String!) :- String!
        self.line_at(envt, (envt.index_of(("\n(decl " + x) + " ") + x.length() + 8).max(0)).replace(")", "")
    # resolve-decl-lookup for the protocol defaults. A name's
    # `:resolves-to` is its refs row in the protocol's piece, else what
    # ensure-references-enriched adds (the prelude module, or `main` for a
    # name declared before any module marker), and the module map row
    # must list it. Only a capitalized name is ever enriched.
    cap(x: String!) :- Bool!
        x.code_at(0) >= 65 and x.code_at(0) <= 90
    rb_s :- rsrc.index_of(("\n(piece " + pc_cur.to_string()) + ")\n")
    rb_t :- self.cut(rsrc, rb_s + 1)
    rblk :- ||: rb_s < 0 : "" ||: rb_t.index_of("\n(piece ") < 0 : rb_t ||: else : rb_t.substring(0, rb_t.index_of("\n(piece ").max(0))
    rrow(x: String!) :- String!
        ||: rblk.index_of((" " + x) + " ") < 0 : "" ||: else : self.line_at(rblk, (rblk.index_of((" " + x) + " ") + x.length() + 2).max(0)).replace(")", "")
    plook(x: String!) :- String!
        ||: pidxt.index_of(("\n" + x) + "|") < 0 : "" ||: else : self.line_at(pidxt, (pidxt.index_of(("\n" + x) + "|") + x.length() + 2).max(0).min(pidxt.length()))
    res(x: String!) :- String!
        ||: self.rrow(x) != "" and self.rrow(x) != "nil" : self.rrow(x) ||: self.plook(x) != "" : self.plook(x) ||: self.in_set(dmain, x) : "main" ||: else : ""
    env_mline(m: String!) :- String!
        self.line_at(envt, (envt.index_of(("\n(module " + m) + " ") + m.length() + 10).max(0))
    env_in_mod(m: String!, x: String!) :- Bool!
        envt.contains(("\n(module " + m) + " ") and (" " + self.env_mline(m).replace(")", " ")).contains((" " + x) + " ")
    hitm(x: String!) :- Bool!
        self.cap(x) and self.res(x) != "" and self.env_in_mod(self.res(x), x)
    hit_enum(x: String!) :- Bool!
        self.env_enum(x) and self.hitm(x)
    e_line(x: String!) :- String!
        self.line_at(envt, (envt.index_of(("\n(enum " + x) + " ") + 1).max(0))
    e_cases(x: String!) :- String!
        self.cut(self.e_line(x), self.e_line(x).index_of("(cases ") + 7).substring(0, self.cut(self.e_line(x), self.e_line(x).index_of("(cases ") + 7).index_of(")").max(0))
    e_case(x: String!, c: String!) :- Bool!
        ((" " + self.e_cases(x)) + " ").contains((" " + c) + " ")
    e_pay(x: String!, c: String!) :- Bool!
        self.e_line(x).contains(("(" + c) + " (params (")
    mangle(m: String!, x: String!) :- String!
        ||: m.starts_with("std.") : "_Cxc_" + x ||: m == "main" : x ||: else : (m.replace(".", "_") + "_") + x
    csafe(x: String!) :- String!
        ||: self.env_has_decl(x) : self.mangle(self.env_decl(x), x) ||: else : x

    # base-type-name, unrolled to depth four (slice 39). An error comes
    # back as `!err:<message>` anywhere in the result.
    nyi(s: String!) :- String!
        "!err:lowering not yet implemented: " + s
    to_outer(t: String!) :- String!
        t.substring(3, (t.index_of("(") - 3).max(0))
    to_inner(t: String!) :- String!
        t.substring((t.index_of("(") + 1).max(0), (t.length() - t.index_of("(") - 2).max(0))
    wr_inner(t: String!) :- String!
        t.substring(3, (t.length() - 4).max(0))
    is_wrap(t: String!) :- Bool!
        t.starts_with("TN(") or t.starts_with("TQ(")
    is_to(t: String!, o: String!) :- Bool!
        t.starts_with("TO:") and self.to_outer(t) == o
    known_outer(t: String!) :- Bool!
        self.is_to(t, "List") or self.is_to(t, "Set") or self.is_to(t, "Ptr") or self.is_to(t, "Map")
    map_kv(t: String!) :- String!
        self.wr_inner(self.to_inner(t))
    map_vt(t: String!) :- String!
        self.cut(self.map_kv(t), self.map_kv(t).index_of(",") + 1)
    map_kok(t: String!) :- Bool!
        self.map_kv(t).index_of(",") > 0 and not self.map_kv(t).substring(0, self.map_kv(t).index_of(",").max(0)).contains("(")
    map_ok(t: String!) :- Bool!
        self.to_inner(t).starts_with("TT(TR:") and self.to_inner(t).ends_with(")") and self.map_kok(t) and (not self.map_vt(t).contains(",") or not self.map_vt(t).starts_with("TR:"))
    map_k(t: String!) :- String!
        self.map_kv(t).substring(3, (self.map_kv(t).index_of(",") - 3).max(0))
    bt_err(t: String!) :- String!
        ||: t == "nil" : self.nyi("base-type-name: unknown type-node ") ||: t.starts_with("TT(") : self.nyi("base-type-name: unknown type-node :type-tuple") ||: t.starts_with("TF(") : self.nyi("base-type-name: unknown type-node :foreign-fn-type") ||: t.starts_with("TO:") and not self.known_outer(t) : self.nyi(("base-type-name: `" + self.to_outer(t)) + " of ...` — only `List of T`, `Map of (K, V)`, `Set of T`, and `Ptr of T` (FFI) supported") ||: else : "!err:port: out of scope"
    bt0(t: String!) :- String!
        ||: t.starts_with("TR:") : t.substring(3, t.length() - 3) ||: else : self.bt_err(t)
    bt1(t: String!) :- String!
        ||: t.starts_with("TR:") : t.substring(3, t.length() - 3) ||: self.is_wrap(t) : self.bt0(self.wr_inner(t)) ||: self.is_to(t, "List") : "_Cxc_ListOf" + self.bt0(self.to_inner(t)) ||: self.is_to(t, "Set") : "_Cxc_SetOf" + self.bt0(self.to_inner(t)) ||: self.is_to(t, "Ptr") : "_Cxc_Ptr_" + self.bt0(self.to_inner(t)) ||: self.is_to(t, "Map") and self.map_ok(t) : ("_Cxc_MapOf" + self.map_k(t)) + self.bt0(self.map_vt(t)) ||: else : self.bt_err(t)
    bt2(t: String!) :- String!
        ||: t.starts_with("TR:") : t.substring(3, t.length() - 3) ||: self.is_wrap(t) : self.bt1(self.wr_inner(t)) ||: self.is_to(t, "List") : "_Cxc_ListOf" + self.bt1(self.to_inner(t)) ||: self.is_to(t, "Set") : "_Cxc_SetOf" + self.bt1(self.to_inner(t)) ||: self.is_to(t, "Ptr") : "_Cxc_Ptr_" + self.bt1(self.to_inner(t)) ||: self.is_to(t, "Map") and self.map_ok(t) : ("_Cxc_MapOf" + self.map_k(t)) + self.bt1(self.map_vt(t)) ||: else : self.bt_err(t)
    bt3(t: String!) :- String!
        ||: t.starts_with("TR:") : t.substring(3, t.length() - 3) ||: self.is_wrap(t) : self.bt2(self.wr_inner(t)) ||: self.is_to(t, "List") : "_Cxc_ListOf" + self.bt2(self.to_inner(t)) ||: self.is_to(t, "Set") : "_Cxc_SetOf" + self.bt2(self.to_inner(t)) ||: self.is_to(t, "Ptr") : "_Cxc_Ptr_" + self.bt2(self.to_inner(t)) ||: self.is_to(t, "Map") and self.map_ok(t) : ("_Cxc_MapOf" + self.map_k(t)) + self.bt2(self.map_vt(t)) ||: else : self.bt_err(t)
    err_of(r: String!) :- String!
        ||: r.contains("!err:") : self.cut(r, r.index_of("!err:") + 5) ||: else : ""
    tkw(t: String!) :- String!
        ||: t.starts_with("TR:") : ":type-ref" ||: t.starts_with("TNT(") : ":type-named-tuple" ||: t.starts_with("TN(") : ":type-nonnil" ||: t.starts_with("TQ(") : ":type-nullable" ||: t.starts_with("TO:") : ":type-of" ||: t.starts_with("TT(") : ":type-tuple" ||: t.starts_with("TF(") : ":foreign-fn-type" ||: else : ""

    # Type keywords as text.
    iserr(t: String!) :- Bool!
        t.starts_with("!")
    is_opt(t: String!) :- Bool!
        t.starts_with("[:optional ")
    unw(t: String!) :- String!
        ||: self.is_opt(t) : t.substring(11, (t.length() - 12).max(0)) ||: else : t
    wrapopt(t: String!) :- String!
        ("[:optional " + t) + "]"
    wrapif(b: Bool!, t: String!) :- String!
        ||: b : self.wrapopt(t) ||: else : t
    ifam(t: String!) :- Bool!
        t == ":int" or t.starts_with("[:int ") or t.starts_with("[:uint ")
    ffam(t: String!) :- Bool!
        t == ":float" or t.starts_with("[:float ")
    num(t: String!) :- Bool!
        self.ifam(t) or self.ffam(t)
    vw(t: String!) :- Int!
        self.ival(self.cut(t, t.index_of(" ") + 1).substring(0, self.cut(t, t.index_of(" ") + 1).index_of("]").max(0)))
    iw(t: String!) :- Int!
        ||: t == ":int" : 64 ||: else : self.vw(t)
    fw(t: String!) :- Int!
        ||: t == ":float" : 64 ||: else : self.vw(t)
    fam(t: String!) :- String!
        ||: t.starts_with("[:uint ") : "uint" ||: else : "int"
    penv(t: String!) :- Bool!
        t == ":int" or t == ":bool" or t == ":float" or t.starts_with("[:int ") or t.starts_with("[:uint ") or t.starts_with("[:float ")
    pr(t: String!) :- String!
        t.replace("~ssize_t", "").replace("~size_t", "")
    sv(t: String!) :- String!
        ||: t == "nil" : "" ||: else : self.pr(t)
    tk_rec(t: String!) :- Bool!
        t.starts_with("{:record \"")
    tk_atom(t: String!) :- Bool!
        t.starts_with("{:atom \"")
    tk_enum(t: String!) :- Bool!
        t.starts_with("{:enum \"")
    tk_nt(t: String!) :- Bool!
        t.starts_with("{:named-tuple \"")
    rec_of(t: String!) :- String!
        t.substring(10, (t.length() - 12).max(0))
    atom_of(t: String!) :- String!
        t.substring(8, (t.length() - 10).max(0))
    nt_of(t: String!) :- String!
        t.substring(15, (t.length() - 17).max(0))
    q_rec(x: String!) :- String!
        ("{:record \"" + x) + "\"}"
    q_atom(x: String!) :- String!
        ("{:atom \"" + x) + "\"}"
    q_enum(x: String!) :- String!
        ("{:enum \"" + x) + "\"}"
    m_user(s: String!) :- String!
        "!U:" + s
    m_nyi(s: String!) :- String!
        "!N:lowering not yet implemented: " + s
    m_unil :- self.m_nyi("unresolved type name `nil`; the type-ref node is missing or wasn't resolved by an earlier pass. Common cause: `List of <Atom>` as a `def Atom(args):` constructor param (not yet supported).")
    is_cont(x: String!) :- Bool!
        x.starts_with("_Cxc_ListOf") or x.starts_with("_Cxc_MapOf") or x.starts_with("_Cxc_SetOf")

    # cxc-type->type-kw.
    tkn(x: String!) :- String!
        ||: self.look(tktab, x) != "" : self.look(tktab, x) ||: x == "nil" : m_unil ||: self.is_rec(x) : self.q_rec(x) ||: self.akey(x) : self.q_atom(x) ||: self.env_enum(x) : ("{:enum \"" + x) + "\"}" ||: x == "SystemPanic" : self.q_atom(x) ||: x.starts_with("_Cxc_NT") : ("{:named-tuple \"" + x) + "\"}" ||: self.is_cont(x) : self.q_atom(x) ||: else : self.m_nyi(("unresolved type name `" + x) + "`")

    # type-kw->cxc-name-str and type-kw->c-type.
    name_str(t: String!) :- String!
        ||: t == ":int" : "Int" ||: t == ":float" : "Double" ||: t == ":string" : "String" ||: t == ":bool" : "Bool" ||: t == ":unit" : "Unit" ||: t == ":never" : "Never" ||: t == ":any" : "Any" ||: t == ":bytes" : "Bytes" ||: t == ":block" : "Block" ||: t.starts_with("[:int ") : "Int" + self.vw(t).to_string() ||: t.starts_with("[:uint ") : "UInt" + self.vw(t).to_string() ||: t.starts_with("[:float ") and self.vw(t) == 32 : "Float" ||: t.starts_with("[:float ") : "Double" ||: self.tk_rec(t) : self.rec_of(t) ||: self.tk_atom(t) or self.tk_enum(t) : self.atom_of(t) ||: else : ""
    opt_name(t: String!) :- String!
        "_Cxc_Optional_" + (||: self.name_str(t) == "Int" : "Int64" ||: else : self.name_str(t))
    ctk(t: String!) :- String!
        ||: self.is_opt(t) : self.opt_name(self.unw(t)) ||: t == ":int" : "int64_t" ||: t == ":float" : "double" ||: t == ":string" : "NSString *" ||: t == ":bool" : "int" ||: t == ":unit" or t == ":never" : "void" ||: t == ":any" : "id" ||: t == ":bytes" : "NSMutableData *" ||: t == ":block" : "void (^)(void)" ||: t.contains("~") : self.cut(t, t.index_of("~") + 1) ||: t.starts_with("[:int ") : ("int" + self.vw(t).to_string()) + "_t" ||: t.starts_with("[:uint ") : ("uint" + self.vw(t).to_string()) + "_t" ||: t.starts_with("[:float ") : "float" ||: t == "[:cstring]" : "const char *" ||: self.tk_rec(t) : self.csafe(self.rec_of(t)) ||: self.tk_atom(t) : self.csafe(self.atom_of(t)) + " *" ||: self.tk_enum(t) : self.csafe(self.atom_of(t)) ||: self.tk_nt(t) : self.nt_of(t) ||: else : self.m_nyi("unrepresentable observable type " + self.pr(t))

    # Self-fields and fields. A `ftab` value is `<cxc-ty>\t<opt|raw>`.
    fkey(k: String!, o: String!, f: String!) :- String!
        ((k + ":") + o) + ("." + f)
    fwrap(v: String!) :- String!
        ||: self.iserr(self.tkn(self.f_first(v))) : self.tkn(self.f_first(v)) ||: self.f_rest(v) == "opt" : self.wrapopt(self.tkn(self.f_first(v))) ||: else : self.tkn(self.f_first(v))
    m_defer(x: String!) :- String!
        self.m_user(("observation-body-deferred: self-observation `" + x) + "` was not typed yet in this pass")
    sf_field(v: String!, x: String!) :- String!
        ||: self.f_first(v) == "nil" : self.m_defer(x) ||: else : self.fwrap(v)
    sf_key(x: String!) :- String!
        ||: sfk == "R" : self.fkey("R", sfo, x) ||: else : self.fkey("A", sfo, x)
    kn_has(x: String!) :- Bool!
        ||: pass == "S" : self.has_key(aobs, (sfo + ".") + x) ||: else : self.has_key(known, x)
    kn_look(x: String!) :- String!
        ||: pass == "S" : self.look(aobs, (sfo + ".") + x) ||: else : self.look(known, x)
    sf_obs(x: String!) :- Bool!
        sfk == "A" and self.kn_has(x)
    sf_hit(x: String!) :- Bool!
        self.sf_obs(x) or self.has_key(ftab, self.sf_key(x))
    sf_tk(x: String!) :- String!
        ||: self.sf_obs(x) and self.kn_look(x) == "nil" : self.m_defer(x) ||: self.sf_obs(x) : self.kn_look(x) ||: else : self.sf_field(self.look(ftab, self.sf_key(x)), x)
    sf_block(x: String!) :- Bool!
        not self.sf_obs(x) and self.f_first(self.look(ftab, self.sf_key(x))) == "Block"
    rw_hit(x: String!) :- Bool!
        sfk == "R" and self.has_key(ftab, self.fkey("R", sfo, x)) and not self.in_set(pnames, x)
    loc_hit(x: String!) :- Bool!
        self.has_key(loc, x) and self.look(loc, x) != "nil"

    # infer-binop-type.
    cmp4(op: String!) :- Bool!
        op == "<" or op == "<=" or op == ">" or op == ">="
    b_ao(l: String!, r: String!) :- Bool!
        self.is_opt(l) or self.is_opt(r)
    b_wf(l: String!, r: String!) :- String!
        ||: self.fw(l) >= self.fw(r) : l ||: else : r
    b_wi(l: String!, r: String!) :- String!
        ||: self.iw(l) >= self.iw(r) : l ||: else : r
    m_mix(op: String!, l: String!, r: String!) :- String!
        self.m_user((("binop " + op) + (" mixes signed " + self.sv(l))) + ((" with unsigned " + self.sv(r)) + " — spec §3.11 requires an explicit conversion"))
    m_btw(op: String!, l: String!, r: String!) :- String!
        self.m_user((("binop " + op) + " between ") + ((self.sv(l) + " and ") + self.sv(r)))
    b_arith(op: String!, l: String!, r: String!, ul: String!, ur: String!) :- String!
        ||: op == "+" and ul == ":string" and ur == ":string" : self.wrapif(self.b_ao(l, r), ":string") ||: self.ffam(ul) and self.ffam(ur) : self.wrapif(self.b_ao(l, r), self.b_wf(ul, ur)) ||: self.ffam(ul) and self.ifam(ur) : self.wrapif(self.b_ao(l, r), ul) ||: self.ifam(ul) and self.ffam(ur) : self.wrapif(self.b_ao(l, r), ur) ||: self.ifam(ul) and self.ifam(ur) and self.fam(ul) != self.fam(ur) : self.m_mix(op, ul, ur) ||: self.ifam(ul) and self.ifam(ur) : self.wrapif(self.b_ao(l, r), self.b_wi(ul, ur)) ||: else : self.m_btw(op, l, r)
    b_res(op: String!, l: String!, r: String!) :- String!
        ||: op == "==" or op == "!=" : ":bool" ||: self.cmp4(op) or op == "and" or op == "or" : self.wrapif(self.b_ao(l, r), ":bool") ||: op == "is" or op == "in" : ":bool" ||: op == "??" : r ||: else : self.b_arith(op, l, r, self.unw(l), self.unw(r))

    # infer-method-call-type, after infer-call-type found a dot callee.
    hint(x: String!) :- String!
        ||: self.look(rhint, x) == "" : "" ||: else : " — available: " + self.look(rhint, x)
    # Which indices a lookup sees. A record pass of the first round has
    # no record index, the first round's record and atom passes no peer
    # atom index, and containers join the atom env after the protocol
    # defaults.
    rpidx :- pass != "R" or rnd == 2
    pidx_ok :- rnd == 2 or pass == "S" or pass == "D"
    cvis :- rnd == 2 and pass != "D"
    own_a(x: String!) :- Bool!
        pass == "A" and x == owner
    mc_rec(x: String!, m: String!) :- String!
        ||: rpidx and self.has_key(rotab, (x + ".") + m) : self.look(rotab, (x + ".") + m) ||: rpidx : self.m_user((("method/observable `" + m) + ("` on record `" + x)) + ("`" + self.hint(x))) ||: else : self.m_user(("method/observable `" + m) + (("` on record `" + x) + "`"))
    # A missing method on an atom carries a mark the error path expands
    # into the sorted names the atom has.
    m_amiss(x: String!, m: String!) :- String!
        self.m_user((("method/observable `" + m) + ("` on atom `" + x)) + (("`" + soh) + ("H" + x)))
    # The slice-42 containers, `C:<class>` to `<kind>\t<elem>` and
    # `<class>.<method>` to `<return>\t<opt|raw>`.
    is_ctn(x: String!) :- Bool!
        cvis and self.has_key(ctab, "C:" + x)
    c_kind(x: String!) :- String!
        ||: self.is_ctn(x) : self.f_first(self.look(ctab, "C:" + x)) ||: else : ""
    c_elem(x: String!) :- String!
        self.f_rest(self.look(ctab, "C:" + x))
    cm_has(x: String!, m: String!) :- Bool!
        cvis and self.has_key(ctab, (x + ".") + m)
    cm_raw(x: String!, m: String!) :- String!
        self.tkn(self.f_first(self.look(ctab, (x + ".") + m)))
    cm_tk(x: String!, m: String!) :- String!
        ||: self.iserr(self.cm_raw(x, m)) : self.cm_raw(x, m) ||: self.f_rest(self.look(ctab, (x + ".") + m)) == "opt" : self.wrapopt(self.cm_raw(x, m)) ||: else : self.cm_raw(x, m)
    l_sug(x: String!, m: String!, sug: Bool!) :- Bool!
        sug and self.c_kind(x) == "list" and (m == "min_by" or m == "max_by" or m == "first")
    sug_tk(x: String!) :- String!
        ||: self.iserr(self.tkn(self.c_elem(x))) : self.tkn(self.c_elem(x)) ||: else : self.wrapopt(self.tkn(self.c_elem(x)))
    mc_atom(x: String!, m: String!) :- String!
        ||: self.cm_has(x, m) : self.cm_tk(x, m) ||: self.in_set(mtab, (x + ".") + m) : m_unil ||: self.own_a(x) and self.has_key(oidx, m) : self.look(oidx, m) ||: self.own_a(x) : self.m_amiss(x, m) ||: self.is_ctn(x) and m == "count" : ":int" ||: pidx_ok and self.has_key(aobs, (x + ".") + m) : self.look(aobs, (x + ".") + m) ||: else : self.m_amiss(x, m)
    int_m(m: String!) :- Bool!
        m == "abs" or m == "min" or m == "max" or m.starts_with("bit") or m == "shl" or m == "shr"
    str_m(m: String!) :- String!
        ||: m == "length" or m == "index_of" or m == "to_int_or" or m == "code_at" or m == "compare_to" : ":int" ||: m == "to_bool_or" or m == "contains" or m == "starts_with" or m == "ends_with" : ":bool" ||: m == "to_double_or" : ":float" ||: m == "to_bytes" : ":bytes" ||: m == "substring" or m == "trim" or m == "replace" or m == "uppercase" or m == "lowercase" : ":string" ||: m == "path_join" or m == "basename" or m == "dirname" or m == "extension" : ":string" ||: m == "trim_prefix" or m == "trim_suffix" or m == "repeat" or m == "pad_left" or m == "pad_right" : ":string" ||: m == "split" : ":string" ||: else : ""
    mc_u(t: String!) :- String!
        self.unw(t)
    mc_prim(t: String!, m: String!) :- String!
        ||: self.mc_u(t) == ":bytes" and m == "at" : ":int" ||: self.mc_u(t) == ":bytes" and m == "slice" : ":bytes" ||: self.mc_u(t) == ":bytes" and m == "to_string" : ":string" ||: self.mc_u(t) == "[:cstring]" and m == "to_string" : ":string" ||: self.ifam(self.mc_u(t)) and (m == "to_string" or m == "to_char_string") : ":string" ||: self.ifam(self.mc_u(t)) and self.int_m(m) : self.wrapif(self.is_opt(t), ":int") ||: self.mc_u(t) == ":bool" and m == "to_string" : ":string" ||: self.mc_u(t) == ":string" and self.str_m(m) != "" : self.str_m(m) ||: else : self.m_user("method call on non-record/non-atom target")
    mc(t: String!, m: String!, na: Bool!, sug: Bool!) :- String!
        ||: self.tk_rec(self.mc_u(t)) and m == "as" and na : ":bytes" ||: self.tk_enum(self.mc_u(t)) and m == "as" and na : ":bytes" ||: self.tk_enum(self.mc_u(t)) and m == "to_string" and na : ":string" ||: self.tk_rec(self.mc_u(t)) : self.mc_rec(self.rec_of(self.mc_u(t)), m) ||: self.tk_atom(self.mc_u(t)) and self.l_sug(self.atom_of(self.mc_u(t)), m, sug) : self.sug_tk(self.atom_of(self.mc_u(t))) ||: self.tk_atom(self.mc_u(t)) : self.mc_atom(self.atom_of(self.mc_u(t)), m) ||: else : self.mc_prim(t, m)

    # field-type-for-owner. A peer atom's untyped observable comes back
    # as `@P<expr>|<atom>` (or `@O` under an Optional owner), which the
    # dot frame types in the peer's context.
    fto_rec(x: String!, f: String!) :- String!
        ||: self.has_key(ftab, self.fkey("R", x, f)) : self.fwrap(self.look(ftab, self.fkey("R", x, f))) ||: rpidx and self.has_key(rotab, (x + ".") + f) : self.look(rotab, (x + ".") + f) ||: else : self.m_user(("field/observable `" + f) + (("` on record `" + x) + "`"))
    raw_obs(x: String!, f: String!) :- String!
        ||: self.look(dtab, "A:" + x) == "" : "" ||: else : self.look(otab, (self.look(dtab, "A:" + x) + ".") + f)
    fto_atom(x: String!, f: String!) :- String!
        ||: self.has_key(ftab, self.fkey("A", x, f)) : self.fwrap(self.look(ftab, self.fkey("A", x, f))) ||: self.own_a(x) and self.has_key(oidx, f) : self.look(oidx, f) ||: self.is_ctn(x) and f == "count" : ":int" ||: pidx_ok and not self.own_a(x) and self.has_key(aobs, (x + ".") + f) : self.look(aobs, (x + ".") + f) ||: self.raw_obs(x, f) != "" : (("@P" + self.raw_obs(x, f)) + "|") + x ||: else : self.m_user(("field/observable `" + f) + (("` on atom `" + x) + "`"))
    fto_agg(t: String!, f: String!) :- String!
        ||: self.tk_rec(t) : self.fto_rec(self.rec_of(t), f) ||: else : self.fto_atom(self.atom_of(t), f)
    fto_opt(r: String!) :- String!
        ||: self.iserr(r) : r ||: r.starts_with("@P") : "@O" + self.cut(r, 2) ||: else : self.wrapopt(self.unw(r))
    m_bytesf(f: String!) :- String!
        self.m_user(("field `" + f) + "` on Bytes — only `.length` ships in F37b L1 (spec §3.10.10). Slice/at/builder methods follow when a use case forces them.")
    m_ntenv(t: String!) :- String!
        self.m_nyi(("named-tuple shape `" + self.nt_of(t)) + "` not found in :named-tuple-env — should have been registered during lowering via collect-shapes")
    fto(t: String!, f: String!) :- String!
        ||: self.is_opt(t) and (self.tk_rec(self.unw(t)) or self.tk_atom(self.unw(t))) : self.fto_opt(self.fto_agg(self.unw(t), f)) ||: t == ":bytes" and f == "length" : ":int" ||: t == ":bytes" : self.m_bytesf(f) ||: self.tk_nt(t) : self.m_ntenv(t) ||: self.tk_rec(t) or self.tk_atom(t) : self.fto_agg(t, f) ||: else : self.m_user("field access on non-aggregate type")
    peer_e(r: String!) :- Int!
        self.ival(r.substring(2, (r.index_of("|") - 2).max(0)))
    peer_a(r: String!) :- String!
        self.cut(r, r.index_of("|") + 1)

    # foreign-type-node->tk.
    fty(t: String!) :- String!
        ||: t.starts_with("TR:") : self.tkn(self.cut(t, 3)) ||: t.starts_with("TN(TR:") : self.tkn(self.cut(self.wr_inner(t), 3)) ||: self.is_to(t, "Ptr") or self.is_to(self.wr_inner(t), "Ptr") : "!N:port: out of scope" ||: t.starts_with("TO:") : self.m_nyi(("FL-7: `" + self.to_outer(t)) + " of ...` unsupported in foreign signature position (only `Ptr of T` at v1.0)") ||: t.starts_with("TN(TO:") : self.m_nyi(("FL-7: `" + self.to_outer(self.wr_inner(t))) + " of ...` unsupported in foreign signature position (only `Ptr of T` at v1.0)") ||: t.starts_with("TN(") : self.m_nyi("FL-3: unknown foreign type-node kind " + self.tkw(self.wr_inner(t))) ||: else : self.m_nyi("FL-3: unknown foreign type-node kind " + self.tkw(t))

    # The typer's frame and the node it is at.
    ftop :- fr.at((fd - 1).max(0)) ?? Frame(n: -1, st: 0, a: "", b: -1, c: "")
    ctx_save :- (sfk + soh) + (sfo + (soh + loc))
    c_sfk(c: String!) :- String!
        c.substring(0, c.index_of(self.soh).max(0))
    c_rest(c: String!) :- String!
        self.cut(c, c.index_of(self.soh) + 1)
    c_sfo(c: String!) :- String!
        self.c_rest(c).substring(0, self.c_rest(c).index_of(self.soh).max(0))
    c_loc(c: String!) :- String!
        self.cut(self.c_rest(c), self.c_rest(c).index_of(self.soh) + 1)
    gh :- self.sx_head(cur)
    gt2 :- self.sx_text(cur + 2)
    # A call's callee and its arguments.
    cc :- cur + 2
    ch :- self.sx_head(cc)
    cnm :- self.sx_text(cc + 2)
    c_na :- self.sx_next(cc) >= self.sx_end(cur)
    c_a1 :- self.sx_next(cc)
    c_a2 :- self.sx_next(c_a1)
    argv(a: Int!) :- Int!
        ||: self.sx_head(a) == "named" : a + 3 ||: else : a + 2
    c_sig :- self.sx_text(cc + 5)
    iv_fref :- ||: c_sig.starts_with("TR:") or c_sig.starts_with("TO:") : self.fty(c_sig) ||: c_sig.starts_with("TF(") : "" ||: else : self.m_nyi("FL-3: unknown foreign signature kind " + self.tkw(c_sig))
    c_cnt :- cnm == "clamp" or cnm == "stackalloc"
    iv_cid :- ||: self.rw_hit(cnm) : self.mc(self.look(loc, "self"), cnm, c_na, false) ||: self.is_rec(cnm) : self.q_rec(cnm) ||: self.akey(cnm) : self.q_atom(cnm) ||: cnm == "print" or cnm == "panic" : ":void" ||: c_cnt : "" ||: self.look(ffit, cnm) != "" : self.look(ffit, cnm) ||: self.sf_block(cnm) : ":void" ||: else : self.m_user(("call to `" + cnm) + "`")
    # (protocol defaults) `E.c(...)` with a payload case and `R.from(...)`
    # resolve once the ctx carries the module map.
    cd_x :- self.sx_text(cc + 4)
    cd_f :- self.sx_text(self.sx_next(cc + 2))
    cd_id :- pass == "D" and self.sx_head(cc + 2) == "ident"
    ep_hit :- cd_id and self.hit_enum(cd_x) and self.e_pay(cd_x, cd_f)
    rf_hit :- cd_id and cd_f == "from" and self.is_rec(cd_x) and self.hitm(cd_x)
    iv_call :- ||: ch == "foreign-ref" : iv_fref ||: ch == "ident" : iv_cid ||: ch == "dot" and ep_hit : self.q_enum(cd_x) ||: ch == "dot" and rf_hit : ("{:decode-outcome \"" + cd_x) + "\"}" ||: ch == "dot" : "" ||: else : self.m_nyi("call with non-ident/non-dot callee " + self.kw(cc))
    m_tident :- self.m_nyi(("type-of identifier `" + gt2) + "` (no local-binding env yet)")
    iv_ident :- ||: self.rw_hit(gt2) : self.fwrap(self.look(ftab, self.fkey("R", sfo, gt2))) ||: self.loc_hit(gt2) : self.look(loc, gt2) ||: self.sf_hit(gt2) : self.sf_tk(gt2) ||: else : m_tident
    m_lam :- self.m_nyi((("lambda expression with " + (self.sx(cur + 2).size - 1).to_string()) + " params — needs a consumer to invoke ") + "through (Layer 5 collection methods `.map`/`.for_each`; will lower to ObjC blocks)")
    m_elist :- "!C:Empty list literal `[]` in expression position has no element type. Corvid needs an element-type context for `[]`, and only field-default position (`xs: List of T = []`) supplies one. In a transition update (`xs => []`), a `let` RHS (`let ys: List of T = []`), or any other assignment position, the parser has no type to attach. Rewrite: use `<field>.empty()` to build a same-typed empty container (e.g. `xs => xs.empty()`; same for `m => m.empty()` on Map and `s => s.empty()` on Set)."
    fr_sym :- self.sx_text(cur + 3).substring(1, (self.sx_text(cur + 3).length() - 2).max(0))
    m_fref :- self.m_nyi(((("FL-3: `plugin.get(\"" + fr_sym) + "\")` used as a value ") + "(not immediately called). MVP FFI lowering only supports the ") + ((("call form `plugin.get(\"" + fr_sym) + "\")(args...)`; ") + "storing the resolved symbol as a function pointer waits on a follow-on landing."))
    g_comp :- gh == "neg" or gh == "not" or gh == "dot" or gh == "subscript" or gh == "chained-cmp"
    g_comp2 :- gh == "do" or gh == "multi-arm" or gh == "foreign-selector-call" or gh == "foreign-class-selector-call"
    g_right :- self.sx_next(cur + 3)
    # (protocol defaults) `E.c` with a case of a resolved enum.
    dt_x :- self.sx_text(cur + 4)
    ec_hit :- pass == "D" and gh == "dot" and self.sx_head(cur + 2) == "ident" and self.hit_enum(dt_x) and self.e_case(dt_x, self.sx_text(self.sx_next(cur + 2)))
    iv_lit :- ||: gh == "int" : ":int" ||: gh == "float" : ":float" ||: gh == "string" : ":string" ||: gh == "bool" : ":bool" ||: gh == "nil" : ":nil" ||: else : ""
    iv :- ||: self.sx(cur).kind != 0 : self.m_nyi("infer-type " + self.kw(cur)) ||: iv_lit != "" : iv_lit ||: gh == "self" and self.loc_hit("self") : self.look(loc, "self") ||: gh == "self" : self.m_user("type-of `self` outside a method body") ||: gh == "ident" : iv_ident ||: gh == "raise" : ":any" ||: gh == "lambda" and self.sx(cur + 2).size == 1 : ":block" ||: gh == "lambda" : m_lam ||: gh == "list" and self.sx(cur).size == 2 : m_elist ||: gh == "list" : self.m_nyi("infer-type :list (non-empty) at this position") ||: gh == "foreign-ref" : m_fref ||: gh == "binop" and self.sx_text(cur + 2) == "is" and self.sx_head(g_right) == "variant" : ":bool" ||: gh == "binop" : "" ||: gh == "call" : iv_call ||: ec_hit : self.q_enum(dt_x) ||: g_comp or g_comp2 : "" ||: else : self.m_nyi("infer-type " + self.kw(cur))
    is_cid :- iv == "" and gh == "call" and ch == "ident"
    # stackalloc's checks.
    sa_v1 :- self.argv(c_a1)
    sa_v2 :- self.argv(c_a2)
    iv_sa :- ||: nac != 2 : self.m_user("stackalloc expects 2 args (TYPE, N-literal), got " + nac.to_string()) ||: self.sx_head(sa_v1) != "ident" : self.m_user("stackalloc first arg must be a bare type identifier (e.g. `Int32`); got " + self.kw(sa_v1)) ||: self.sx_head(sa_v2) != "int" : self.m_user("stackalloc second arg must be a compile-time integer literal (fixed array length); got " + self.kw(sa_v2)) ||: self.ival(self.sx_text(sa_v2 + 2)) <= 0 : self.m_user("stackalloc length must be a positive integer, got " + self.sx_text(sa_v2 + 2)) ||: self.iserr(self.tkn(self.sx_text(sa_v1 + 2))) : self.tkn(self.sx_text(sa_v1 + 2)) ||: else : "!N:port: out of scope"
    # Stage results on return.
    t_n :- ftop.n
    u_head :- self.sx_head(t_n)
    un_res :- ||: u_head == "not" : self.wrapif(self.is_opt(val), ":bool") ||: u_head == "subscript" and val == ":string" : ":int" ||: u_head == "subscript" : self.m_user(("subscript `expr[i]` on target of type " + self.pr(val)) + " — F19 L2 handles `String[i]` only. List / Map indexing waits on F42 (from_literal) + F43 (container-as-atom); use `.get`/`.contains` for now.") ||: self.num(self.unw(val)) : val ||: else : self.m_user("unary minus on non-numeric type " + self.pr(val))
    d_res :- self.fto(val, self.sx_text(self.sx_next(t_n + 2)))
    m_cdot :- t_n + 2
    m_a1 :- self.sx_next(m_cdot)
    m_sug :- m_a1 < self.sx_end(t_n) and self.sx_next(m_a1) >= self.sx_end(t_n) and self.sx_head(self.argv(m_a1)) == "lambda"
    m_res :- self.mc(val, self.sx_text(self.sx_next(m_cdot + 2)), m_a1 >= self.sx_end(t_n), m_sug)
    ch_flag :- ftop.a == "1" or self.is_opt(val)
    ch_next :- self.sx_next(ftop.b)
    ch_a :- ||: ch_flag : "1" ||: else : "0"
    # The do-block step, at the statement `ftop.b` of the block.
    ds_k :- ftop.b
    ds_h :- self.sx_head(ds_k)
    ds_ty :- self.sx_text(ds_k + 3)
    ds_ann :- ||: self.err_of(self.bt3(ds_ty)) != "" : "!N:" + self.err_of(self.bt3(ds_ty)) ||: else : self.tkn(self.bt3(ds_ty))
    ds_done :- ds_k >= self.sx_end(t_n)
    ds_last :- self.ival(ftop.a)
    ds_eval :- (ds_h == "let" and ds_ty == "nil") or ds_h == "alias"
    ds_expr :- ||: ds_h == "let" : ds_k + 4 ||: else : ds_k + 3
    tf_c :- ||: tfp >= tfs.length() : -1 ||: else : tfs.code_at(tfp)
    tf_ret :- tfs.substring((tfp + 1).min(tfs.length()), (tfs.length() - tfp - 2).max(0))
    # try-infer-observation-body's three deferred user errors.
    df_msg :- self.cut(terr, 3)
    df_tail :- self.cut(self.cut(df_msg, 19), self.cut(df_msg, 19).index_of("`"))
    df_meth :- df_msg.starts_with("method/observable `") and df_tail.starts_with("` on atom `")
    df_cont :- df_msg.contains("on atom `_Cxc_ListOf") or df_msg.contains("on atom `_Cxc_MapOf") or df_msg.contains("on atom `_Cxc_SetOf")
    deferred :- terr.starts_with("!U:") and (df_cont or df_msg.starts_with("observation-body-deferred:") or df_meth)

    # One observable, `(obs <name> (params ...) <ret>|nil <expr> ...)` at oi.
    o_name :- self.sx_text(oi + 2)
    o_ret :- self.sx_text(self.sx_next(oi + 3))
    o_expr :- self.sx_next(self.sx_next(oi + 3))
    q_ty :- ||: self.sx_head(qk) == "field" : self.sx_text(qk + 3) ||: else : "nil"
    q_nm :- ||: self.sx_head(qk) == "field" : self.sx_text(qk + 2) ||: else : "self"
    q_tn :- ||: q_ty.starts_with("TR:") : self.cut(q_ty, 3) ||: q_ty.starts_with("TN(TR:") : self.cut(self.wr_inner(q_ty), 3) ||: else : "nil"
    q_tk :- ||: self.iserr(self.tkn(q_tn)) : self.tkn(q_tn) ||: not q_ty.starts_with("TN(") and self.penv(self.tkn(q_tn)) : self.wrapopt(self.tkn(q_tn)) ||: else : self.tkn(q_tn)
    o_bt :- self.bt3(o_ret)
    o_dk :- ||: self.err_of(o_bt) != "" : "!N:" + self.err_of(o_bt) ||: self.iserr(self.tkn(o_bt)) : self.tkn(o_bt) ||: not o_ret.starts_with("TN(") and self.penv(self.tkn(o_bt)) : self.wrapopt(self.tkn(o_bt)) ||: else : self.tkn(o_bt)
    o_ct :- ||: otk == "nil" : "nil" ||: else : self.ctk(otk)
    o_ctq :- ||: otk == "nil" : "nil" ||: else : ("\"" + o_ct) + "\""
    o_row :- (("(obs " + owner) + (" " + o_name)) + ((" " + self.pr(otk)) + ((" " + o_ctq) + ")"))
    self_tk :- ||: pass == "R" : self.q_rec(owner) ||: else : self.q_atom(owner)
    o_fail :- ||: self.iserr(otk) : otk ||: else : o_ct
    o_msg :- self.cut(o_fail, 3)

    # The sections an error follows. In round2 the first round prints
    # none of its own.
    epre :- ||: mode == "round2" and rnd == 1 : "" ||: else : rsec
    # The post rows. An error with no companion section before it came
    # before the protocol defaults (the demand, the parity check), one
    # after the companion section comes from the container synthesis.
    p_ei :- postt.index_of("\nerror|")
    p_err :- p_ei >= 0
    p_errl :- self.line_at(postt, (p_ei + 1).max(0))
    p_pre :- p_err and not postt.substring(0, p_ei.max(0)).contains("\n(companions ")
    # One protocol row at gi, one of its defaults at oi,
    # `(default <name> (params ...) <ret>|nil <type>|nil <expr>)`.
    pd_dl :- self.sx_next(self.sx_next(gi + 3))
    pd_pn :- self.sx_text(gi + 2)
    pd_ret :- self.sx_text(self.sx_next(oi + 3))
    pd_expr :- self.sx_next(self.sx_next(self.sx_next(oi + 3)))
    pd_row(r: String!) :- String!
        (("(pdefault " + pd_pn) + (" " + self.sx_text(oi + 2))) + ((" " + r) + ")")
    pd_nm :- ||: terr == "" and self.name_str(val) != "" : self.name_str(val) ||: else : "nil"
    pd_ok :- terr == "" or terr.starts_with("!N:")
    # The mark of a missing method on an atom, and the names to list.
    hx_i :- ferr.index_of(soh + "H")
    hx_x :- self.cut(ferr, hx_i + 2)
    hx_base :- ferr.substring(0, hx_i.max(0))
    hx_tab :- ||: self.is_ctn(hx_x) : ctab ||: self.own_a(hx_x) : oidx ||: pidx_ok : aobs ||: else : ""
    hx_pre :- ||: self.own_a(hx_x) : "" ||: else : hx_x + "."
    hx_ln :- self.line_at(hx_t, gi)
    hx_nm :- self.f_first(self.cut(hx_ln, pown.length()))
    # NSString's hasPrefix: is false for an empty prefix.
    hx_take :- hx_ln != "" and (pown == "" or hx_ln.starts_with(pown)) and not rows.contains(hx_nm)
    hx_list :- ||: nsorted == 0 : "" ||: else : " — available: " + self.cut(sorted, 1).replace("\n", ", ")

    # Prep. The current top form and its children.
    gh0 :- self.sx_head(gi)
    gn0 :- self.sx_text(gi + 2)
    g1_more :- gh0 == "enum" or gh0 == "module" or gh0 == "piece" or gh0 == "protocol"
    # A slice-42 container row `(container <class> <kind> <elem> ...)`,
    # its `(methods (m <name> <param>* <ret> opt|raw)*)` and a List's
    # `(fanin-payloads (<stream> <arg>*)*)`.
    c_kd :- self.sx_text(gi + 3)
    c_meth :- ||: c_kd == "map" : gi + 6 ||: else : gi + 5
    c_fanp :- self.sx_next(self.sx_next(self.sx_next(gi + 5)))
    s_end :- self.sx_end(0)
    p_head :- self.sx_head(pj)
    p_obs :- self.sx_head(pj) == "obs"
    # A field row `(f <name> <cxc-ty> bang|plain opt|raw ...)`.
    p_frow :- self.sx_text(pj + 3) + ("\t" + self.sx_text(pj + 5))

    # Owners.
    own_at(i: Int!) :- String!
        ||: pass == "R" : recl.at(i) ?? "" ||: else : atl.at(i) ?? ""
    own_n :- ||: pass == "R" : recl.count() ||: else : atl.count()
    own_ok :- self.look(dtab, (pass + ":") + self.own_at(pk)) != ""
    own_def :- self.ival(self.look(dtab, (pass + ":") + self.own_at(pk)))
    own_first :- ||: pass == "R" : own_def + 3 ||: else : self.sx_next(self.sx_next(own_def + 3))

    # The stream pass. The atom row, its ctor params, and its transitions.
    w_row :- self.ival(self.look(dtab, "W:" + owner))
    w_ctor :- self.sx_next(w_row + 3)
    w_trs :- self.sx_next(self.sx_next(self.sx_next(self.sx_next(w_ctor))))
    c_tk :- self.tkn(self.sx_text(qk + 3))
    # A transition `(transition <line> <src> <recv>|nil <target> <clause>*)`.
    t_recv(t: Int!) :- Int!
        self.sx_next(t + 3)
    t_tgt(t: Int!) :- String!
        self.sx_text(self.sx_next(self.t_recv(t)))
    t_c0(t: Int!) :- Int!
        self.sx_next(self.sx_next(self.t_recv(t)))
    t_hasr :- self.sx_head(self.t_recv(oi)) == "recv"
    t_wild :- self.sx_text(oi + 3) == "implicit" and not t_hasr
    t_msg :- self.t_recv(oi) + 3
    p_end :- ||: t_hasr : self.sx_end(t_msg) ||: else : 0
    p_first :- ||: t_hasr and self.sx_head(t_msg) == "typed" : t_msg + 3 ||: t_hasr and self.sx_head(t_msg) == "src" : self.sx_next(t_msg + 2) ||: else : p_end
    p_bt :- self.bt3(self.sx_text(qk + 3))
    p_tk :- ||: self.err_of(p_bt) != "" : "!N:" + self.err_of(p_bt) ||: else : self.tkn(p_bt)
    a_stend :- self.sx_end(self.sx_next(qk + 2))
    is_semit :- self.sx(pj).kind == 0 and self.sx_head(pj) == "emit" and self.sx_text(pj + 3) == "nil"
    od_tk :- ||: terr == "" : val ||: else : "nil"
    # The reduce over the sites. A site is `<stream>\n` and one
    # `<key>\t<type-kw>\n` line per arg, `sacc` the args still to visit,
    # `sprev` the first site's type keywords, each ended by the soh char.
    s_cur :- sites.at(qk) ?? ""
    s_stream :- self.line_at(s_cur, 0)
    s_args :- self.cut(s_cur, s_stream.length() + 1)
    sa_line :- self.line_at(sacc, 0)
    sa_k :- self.f_first(sa_line)
    sa_tk :- self.f_rest(sa_line)
    sa_ct :- self.ctk(sa_tk)
    sp_tk :- sprev.substring(0, sprev.index_of(self.soh).max(0))
    m_incon :- self.m_nyi((("def-atom `" + owner) + ("` emits stream `" + s_stream)) + ((("` with inconsistent type on key `" + sa_k) + ("`: previously " + self.pr(sp_tk))) + ((", here " + self.pr(sa_tk)) + "; every emit of the same stream must agree on payload key types")))

    # Sorting.
    scan_cur :- rows.at(sort_i) ?? ""
    scan_cmp :- scan_cur.compare_to(scan_best)
    s_done   :- sort_i >= rows.count() and not scan_has
    s_left   :- rows.filter(e => e != scan_best)
    s_cnt    :- rows.count() - s_left.count()

    -> reading
        then:
            mode => args.get_or(1, "")
            self :> start

    -> prep
        then: self :> g0

    -> sorting
        then: self :> scan

    -> done
        then: self :> fin

    -> end
        then: console.write(self.cut(out, 1))

    done <: fin -> end

    reading <: start -> reading
        then:
            let raw: String! = fs.read_text(args.get_or(2, ""))
            let rws: String! = fs.read_text(args.get_or(3, ""))
            let body: String! = ||: raw.ends_with("\n") : raw.substring(0, (raw.length() - 1).max(0)) ||: else : raw
            let pst: String! = ||: mode == "round2" : "\n" + fs.read_text(args.get_or(5, "")) ||: else : "\n"
            let pcl: String! = ||: pst.contains("\nerror|") : pst.substring(0, pst.index_of("\nerror|").max(0)) ||: else : pst
            envt => ("\n" + rws) + "\n"
            src => (body + ("\n" + rws)) + pcl
            ffit => "\n" + fs.read_text(args.get_or(4, ""))
            postt => pst
            pidxt => ||: mode == "round2" : "\n" + fs.read_text(args.get_or(6, "")) ||: else : ""
            rsrc => ||: mode == "round2" : "\n" + fs.read_text(args.get_or(7, "")) ||: else : ""
            self :> chk

    # An error from slice 40 or earlier passes through.
    reading <: chk -> done
        |: env_err
        then:
            out => "\n" + env_errl

    reading <: chk -> done
        |: not env_err and src.starts_with("error|")
        then:
            out => "\n" + self.line_at(src, 0)

    reading <: chk -> reading
        |: not env_err and not src.starts_with("error|")
        then: self :> rd

    reading <: rd -> prep
        |: rmode == 0 and r_end
        then:
            nodes => nodes.sort_by(n => n.pre)

    reading <: rd -> reading
        |: rmode == 0 and r_sp
        then:
            rp => rp + 1
            self :> rd

    reading <: rd -> reading
        |: rmode == 0 and r_open
        then:
            rstack => rstack.slice(0, sp).append(SNode(pre: ncount, kind: 0, start: rp, stop: 0, depth: sp, size: 0, parent: r_parent))
            ncount => ncount + 1
            sp => sp + 1
            rp => rp + 1
            self :> rd

    reading <: rd -> reading
        |: rmode == 0 and r_close
        then:
            nodes => nodes.append(SNode(pre: rtop.pre, kind: 0, start: rtop.start, stop: rp + 1, depth: rtop.depth, size: ncount - rtop.pre, parent: rtop.parent))
            sp => (sp - 1).max(0)
            rp => rp + 1
            self :> rd

    reading <: rd -> reading
        |: rmode == 0 and r_quote
        then:
            tstart => rp
            rmode => 2
            rp => rp + 1
            self :> rd

    reading <: rd -> reading
        |: rmode == 0 and r_plain and not r_quote
        then:
            tstart => rp
            rmode => 1
            rnest => 0
            rp => rp + 1
            self :> rd

    reading <: rd -> reading
        |: rmode == 1 and a_stop
        then:
            nodes => nodes.append(SNode(pre: ncount, kind: 1, start: tstart, stop: rp, depth: sp, size: 1, parent: r_parent))
            ncount => ncount + 1
            rmode => 0
            self :> rd

    reading <: rd -> reading
        |: rmode == 1 and not a_stop and r_open
        then:
            rnest => rnest + 1
            rp => rp + 1
            self :> rd

    reading <: rd -> reading
        |: rmode == 1 and not a_stop and r_close
        then:
            rnest => rnest - 1
            rp => rp + 1
            self :> rd

    reading <: rd -> reading
        |: rmode == 1 and not a_stop and not r_open and not r_close
        then:
            rp => rp + 1
            self :> rd

    reading <: rd -> reading
        |: rmode == 2 and (r_quote or r_end)
        then:
            nodes => nodes.append(SNode(pre: ncount, kind: 2, start: tstart, stop: (rp + 1).min(src.length()), depth: sp, size: 1, parent: r_parent))
            ncount => ncount + 1
            rmode => 0
            rp => rp + 1
            self :> rd

    reading <: rd -> reading
        |: rmode == 2 and not r_end and not r_quote and r_bs
        then:
            rmode => 3
            rp => rp + 1
            self :> rd

    reading <: rd -> reading
        |: rmode == 2 and not r_end and not r_quote and not r_bs
        then:
            rp => rp + 1
            self :> rd

    reading <: rd -> reading
        |: rmode == 3
        then:
            rmode => 2
            rp => (rp + 1).min(src.length())
            self :> rd

    # Prep, the stream's top nodes. The last record or agent of a name is
    # the one its env entry came from. An agent's observables index by
    # node, the first of a name winning (field-type-for-owner's `some`).
    prep <: g0 -> prep
        then:
            gi => 2
            self :> g1

    prep <: g1 -> prep
        |: gi < s_end and gh0 == "record"
        then:
            dtab => self.put_last(dtab, "R:" + gn0, gi.to_string())
            dmain => ||: cur_mod == "main" : dmain + (gn0 + "\n") ||: else : dmain
            gi => self.sx_next(gi)
            self :> g1

    prep <: g1 -> prep
        |: gi < s_end and gh0 == "agent"
        then:
            dtab => self.put_last(dtab, "A:" + gn0, gi.to_string())
            dmain => ||: cur_mod == "main" : dmain + (gn0 + "\n") ||: else : dmain
            pj => self.sx_next(self.sx_next(gi + 3))
            pe => self.sx_end(gi)
            self :> g2

    # (round2) Module and piece markers, enums for the main-module names
    # of the ensure fallback, and the piece of each protocol.
    prep <: g1 -> prep
        |: gi < s_end and g1_more
        then:
            dmain => ||: gh0 == "enum" and cur_mod == "main" : dmain + (gn0 + "\n") ||: else : dmain
            cur_mod => ||: gh0 == "module" : gn0 ||: else : cur_mod
            pcn => ||: gh0 == "piece" : pcn + 1 ||: else : pcn
            dtab => ||: gh0 == "protocol" : self.put_last(dtab, "P:" + gn0, pcn.to_string()) ||: else : dtab
            gi => self.sx_next(gi)
            self :> g1

    prep <: g1 -> prep
        |: gi < s_end and gh0 != "record" and gh0 != "agent" and not g1_more
        then:
            gi => self.sx_next(gi)
            self :> g1

    prep <: g1 -> prep
        |: gi >= s_end
        then:
            gi => s_end
            self :> g3

    prep <: g2 -> prep
        |: pj < pe
        then:
            otab => ||: p_obs : self.put_first(otab, (gi.to_string() + ".") + self.sx_text(pj + 2), self.sx_next(self.sx_next(pj + 3)).to_string()) ||: else : otab
            pj => self.sx_next(pj)
            self :> g2

    prep <: g2 -> prep
        |: pj >= pe
        then:
            gi => self.sx_next(gi)
            self :> g1

    # The env rows after the stream. A kept atom's fields and handler
    # methods, a record's fields.
    prep <: g3 -> prep
        |: gi < nn and gh0 == "atom" and self.akey(gn0)
        then:
            atl => atl.append(gn0)
            dtab => self.put_last(dtab, "W:" + gn0, gi.to_string())
            pown => gn0
            pj => gi + 5
            pe => self.sx_end(gi + 3)
            self :> g4

    prep <: g3 -> prep
        |: gi < nn and gh0 == "record"
        then:
            recl => recl.append(gn0)
            pown => gn0
            pj => self.sx_next(gi + 3) + 2
            pe => self.sx_end(self.sx_next(gi + 3))
            self :> g6

    prep <: g3 -> prep
        |: gi < nn and gh0 == "protocol"
        then:
            prl => prl.append(gi)
            gi => self.sx_next(gi)
            self :> g3

    prep <: g3 -> prep
        |: gi < nn and gh0 == "container"
        then:
            ctab => self.put_last(ctab, "C:" + gn0, (c_kd + "\t") + self.sx_text(gi + 4))
            cobs => cobs.append(("(obs " + gn0) + " count :int nil)")
            pown => gn0
            pj => c_meth + 2
            pe => self.sx_end(c_meth)
            self :> g7

    prep <: g3 -> prep
        |: gi < nn and gh0 != "record" and (gh0 != "atom" or not self.akey(gn0)) and gh0 != "protocol" and gh0 != "container"
        then:
            gi => self.sx_next(gi)
            self :> g3

    prep <: g7 -> prep
        |: pj < pe
        then:
            ctab => self.put_last(ctab, (pown + ".") + self.sx_text(pj + 2), (self.sx_text(self.sx_end(pj) - 2) + "\t") + self.sx_text(self.sx_end(pj) - 1))
            pj => self.sx_next(pj)
            self :> g7

    prep <: g7 -> prep
        |: pj >= pe and c_kd == "list"
        then:
            pj => c_fanp + 2
            pe => self.sx_end(c_fanp)
            self :> g8

    prep <: g7 -> prep
        |: pj >= pe and c_kd != "list"
        then:
            gi => self.sx_next(gi)
            self :> g3

    prep <: g8 -> prep
        |: pj < pe
        then:
            cspi => cspi.append(("(spi " + pown) + (" " + self.cut(self.sx_text(pj), 1)))
            pj => self.sx_next(pj)
            self :> g8

    prep <: g8 -> prep
        |: pj >= pe
        then:
            gi => self.sx_next(gi)
            self :> g3

    prep <: g3 -> pass
        |: gi >= nn
        then:
            pass => "R"
            pk => 0
            self :> ow

    prep <: g4 -> prep
        |: pj < pe
        then:
            ftab => self.put_last(ftab, self.fkey("A", pown, self.sx_text(pj + 2)), p_frow)
            pj => self.sx_next(pj)
            self :> g4

    prep <: g4 -> prep
        |: pj >= pe
        then:
            pj => self.sx_next(self.sx_next(gi + 3)) + 2
            pe => self.sx_end(self.sx_next(self.sx_next(gi + 3)))
            self :> g5

    prep <: g5 -> prep
        |: pj < pe
        then:
            mtab => mtab + (((pown + ".") + self.sx_text(pj + 2)) + "\n")
            pj => self.sx_next(pj)
            self :> g5

    prep <: g5 -> prep
        |: pj >= pe
        then:
            gi => self.sx_next(gi)
            self :> g3

    prep <: g6 -> prep
        |: pj < pe
        then:
            ftab => self.put_last(ftab, self.fkey("R", pown, self.sx_text(pj + 2)), p_frow)
            pj => self.sx_next(pj)
            self :> g6

    prep <: g6 -> prep
        |: pj >= pe
        then:
            gi => self.sx_next(gi)
            self :> g3

    # The passes. One owner at a time, then its items.
    pass <: ow -> pass
        |: pk < own_n
        then:
            owner => self.own_at(pk)
            oi => ||: own_ok : own_first ||: else : 0
            oe => ||: own_ok : self.sx_end(own_def) ||: else : 0
            known => "\n"
            oidx => "\n"
            self :> it

    pass <: ow -> sorting
        |: pk >= own_n
        then:
            rows => ||: pass == "A" and rnd == 2 : orows.concat(cobs) ||: else : orows
            orows => orows.empty()
            sort_ret => pass

    pass <: it -> pass
        |: oi < oe and self.sx_head(oi) == "obs"
        then:
            loc => "\n"
            pnames => "\n"
            qk => oi + 5
            self :> pq

    pass <: it -> pass
        |: oi < oe and self.sx_head(oi) != "obs"
        then:
            oi => self.sx_next(oi)
            self :> it

    pass <: it -> pass
        |: oi >= oe and (pass == "A" or rows.count() == 0)
        then:
            pk => pk + 1
            rows => rows.empty()
            self :> ow

    # A record's observable names, sorted once its pass is done, are the
    # hint of a later missing-method message.
    pass <: it -> sorting
        |: oi >= oe and pass == "R" and rows.count() > 0
        then:
            sort_ret => "hint"

    # The param locals, then the declared type or the typer.
    pass <: pq -> pass
        |: qk < self.sx_end(oi + 3) and not self.iserr(q_tk)
        then:
            loc => self.put_last(loc, q_nm, q_tk)
            pnames => pnames + (q_nm + "\n")
            qk => self.sx_next(qk)
            self :> pq

    pass <: pq -> pass
        |: qk < self.sx_end(oi + 3) and self.iserr(q_tk)
        then:
            otk => q_tk
            self :> fn

    pass <: pq -> pass
        |: qk >= self.sx_end(oi + 3) and o_ret != "nil"
        then:
            loc => self.put_last(loc, "self", self_tk)
            otk => o_dk
            self :> fn

    pass <: pq -> ty
        |: qk >= self.sx_end(oi + 3) and o_ret == "nil"
        then:
            loc => self.put_last(loc, "self", self_tk)
            fd => 0
            cur => o_expr
            sfk => pass
            sfo => owner
            terr => ""
            nac => -1
            sret => "o"
            self :> go

    pass <: od -> pass
        |: sret == "o"
        then:
            otk => ||: terr == "" : val ||: deferred and rnd == 1 : "nil" ||: else : terr
            self :> fn

    pass <: fn -> pass
        |: self.iserr(o_fail)
        then:
            ferr => o_msg
            fpre => ||: pass == "R" and rnd == 1 : "" ||: else : epre
            self :> hx

    pass <: fn -> pass
        |: not self.iserr(o_fail)
        then:
            orows => orows.append(o_row)
            rotab => ||: pass == "R" and rnd == 1 : self.put_last(rotab, (owner + ".") + o_name, otk) ||: else : rotab
            rotab2 => ||: pass == "R" and rnd == 2 : self.put_last(rotab2, (owner + ".") + o_name, otk) ||: else : rotab2
            rows => ||: pass == "R" and rnd == 1 and not rows.contains(o_name) : rows.append(o_name) ||: else : rows
            known => self.put_last(known, o_name, otk)
            aobs => ||: pass == "A" and rnd == 1 : self.put_last(aobs, (owner + ".") + o_name, otk) ||: else : aobs
            aobs2 => ||: pass == "A" and rnd == 2 : self.put_last(aobs2, (owner + ".") + o_name, otk) ||: else : aobs2
            oidx => ||: otk != "nil" : self.put_last(oidx, o_name, otk) ||: else : oidx
            oi => self.sx_next(oi)
            self :> it

    # The error path. A missing method on an atom lists the sorted names
    # the atom has (its handler methods, then its observable index or
    # its container methods with `count` and the list sugars).
    pass <: hx -> done
        |: hx_i < 0
        then:
            out => fpre + ("\nerror|" + ferr)

    pass <: hx -> pass
        |: hx_i >= 0
        then:
            rows => rows.empty()
            hx_t => mtab
            pown => hx_x + "."
            gi => 0
            pj => 1
            self :> hs

    pass <: hs -> pass
        |: gi < hx_t.length()
        then:
            rows => ||: hx_take : rows.append(hx_nm) ||: else : rows
            gi => gi + hx_ln.length() + 1
            self :> hs

    pass <: hs -> pass
        |: gi >= hx_t.length() and pj == 1
        then:
            hx_t => hx_tab
            pown => hx_pre
            gi => 0
            pj => 2
            self :> hs

    pass <: hs -> sorting
        |: gi >= hx_t.length() and pj == 2
        then:
            rows => ||: self.c_kind(hx_x) == "list" : rows.append("count").append("first").append("max_by").append("min_by") ||: self.is_ctn(hx_x) : rows.append("count") ||: else : rows
            sort_ret => "H"

    # (round2) infer-protocol-defaults, after the first round and the
    # steps the post rows stand for (the demand, the parity check).
    pass <: pd0 -> done
        |: p_pre
        then:
            out => "\n" + p_errl

    pass <: pd0 -> pass
        |: not p_pre
        then:
            pk => 0
            orows => orows.empty()
            pass => "D"
            self :> pa

    pass <: pa -> pass
        |: pk < prl.count()
        then:
            gi => prl.at(pk) ?? 0
            self :> pc

    pass <: pc -> pass
        then:
            pc_cur => self.ival(self.look(dtab, "P:" + pd_pn))
            oi => pd_dl + 2
            oe => self.sx_end(pd_dl)
            self :> pb

    pass <: pa -> sorting
        |: pk >= prl.count()
        then:
            rows => orows
            orows => orows.empty()
            sort_ret => "D"

    pass <: pb -> pass
        |: oi < oe and pd_ret != "nil"
        then:
            orows => orows.append(self.pd_row(pd_ret))
            oi => self.sx_next(oi)
            self :> pb

    pass <: pb -> ty
        |: oi < oe and pd_ret == "nil"
        then:
            fd => 0
            cur => pd_expr
            sfk => "D"
            sfo => ""
            loc => "\n"
            terr => ""
            nac => -1
            sret => "d"
            self :> go

    pass <: pb -> pass
        |: oi >= oe
        then:
            pk => pk + 1
            self :> pa

    pass <: od -> pass
        |: sret == "d" and pd_ok
        then:
            orows => orows.append(self.pd_row(pd_nm))
            oi => self.sx_next(oi)
            self :> pb

    pass <: od -> pass
        |: sret == "d" and not pd_ok
        then:
            ferr => self.cut(terr, 3)
            fpre => ""
            self :> hx

    # The stream pass, infer-streams-in-atom-env. Per atom the ctor locals
    # (built for every atom, an error aborts), then per transition its
    # context, the alias heads of its `then` clauses, and its untargeted
    # emits, an arg the typer cannot type leaving its site out. The sites
    # are then reduced by stream, the first giving the C types.
    pass <: xa -> pass
        |: pk < atl.count()
        then:
            owner => atl.at(pk) ?? ""
            cloc => "\n"
            sites => sites.empty()
            stab => "\n"
            self :> xb

    pass <: xa -> sorting
        |: pk >= atl.count()
        then:
            rows => ||: rnd == 2 : orows.concat(cspi) ||: else : orows
            orows => orows.empty()
            sort_ret => "S"

    pass <: xb -> pass
        then:
            qk => w_ctor + 2
            self :> xc

    pass <: xc -> pass
        |: qk < self.sx_end(w_ctor) and not self.iserr(c_tk)
        then:
            cloc => self.put_last(cloc, self.sx_text(qk + 2), c_tk)
            qk => self.sx_next(qk)
            self :> xc

    pass <: xc -> done
        |: qk < self.sx_end(w_ctor) and self.iserr(c_tk)
        then:
            out => epre + ("\nerror|" + self.cut(c_tk, 3))

    pass <: xc -> pass
        |: qk >= self.sx_end(w_ctor)
        then:
            oi => w_trs + 2
            oe => self.sx_end(w_trs)
            tinit => ||: w_trs + 2 < self.sx_end(w_trs) : self.t_tgt(w_trs + 2) ||: else : "init"
            self :> xt

    pass <: xt -> pass
        |: oi < oe and t_wild
        then:
            tloc => ||: self.t_tgt(oi) == tinit : self.put_last(cloc, "self", self_tk) ||: else : self.put_last("\n", "self", self_tk)
            qk => self.t_c0(oi)
            self :> xf

    pass <: xt -> pass
        |: oi < oe and not t_wild
        then:
            tloc => self.put_last("\n", "self", self_tk)
            qk => p_first
            self :> xp

    pass <: xt -> pass
        |: oi >= oe
        then:
            qk => 0
            self :> xr

    pass <: xp -> pass
        |: qk < p_end and not self.iserr(p_tk)
        then:
            tloc => self.put_last(tloc, self.sx_text(qk + 2), p_tk)
            qk => self.sx_next(qk)
            self :> xp

    pass <: xp -> done
        |: qk < p_end and self.iserr(p_tk)
        then:
            out => epre + ("\nerror|" + self.cut(p_tk, 3))

    pass <: xp -> pass
        |: qk >= p_end
        then:
            qk => self.t_c0(oi)
            self :> xf

    pass <: xf -> pass
        |: qk < self.sx_end(oi) and self.sx_head(qk) == "then"
        then:
            pj => self.sx_next(qk + 2) + 2
            self :> xg

    pass <: xf -> pass
        |: qk < self.sx_end(oi) and self.sx_head(qk) != "then"
        then:
            qk => self.sx_next(qk)
            self :> xf

    pass <: xf -> pass
        |: qk >= self.sx_end(oi)
        then:
            pj => oi + 1
            pe => self.sx_end(oi)
            self :> xe

    pass <: xg -> ty
        |: pj < a_stend and self.sx_head(pj) == "alias"
        then:
            fd => 0
            cur => pj + 3
            sfk => "A"
            sfo => owner
            loc => tloc
            terr => ""
            nac => -1
            sret => "a"
            self :> go

    pass <: xg -> pass
        |: pj >= a_stend or self.sx_head(pj) != "alias"
        then:
            qk => self.sx_next(qk)
            self :> xf

    pass <: od -> pass
        |: sret == "a"
        then:
            tloc => ||: terr == "" and val != "nil" : self.put_last(tloc, self.sx_text(pj + 2), val) ||: else : tloc
            pj => self.sx_next(pj)
            self :> xg

    pass <: xe -> pass
        |: pj < pe and is_semit
        then:
            sacc => self.sx_text(pj + 4) + "\n"
            gi => pj + 5
            self :> xy

    pass <: xe -> pass
        |: pj < pe and not is_semit
        then:
            pj => pj + 1
            self :> xe

    pass <: xe -> pass
        |: pj >= pe
        then:
            oi => self.sx_next(oi)
            self :> xt

    pass <: xy -> ty
        |: gi < self.sx_end(pj)
        then:
            fd => 0
            cur => self.argv(gi)
            sfk => "A"
            sfo => owner
            loc => tloc
            terr => ""
            nac => -1
            sret => "e"
            self :> go

    pass <: xy -> pass
        |: gi >= self.sx_end(pj)
        then:
            sites => ||: sacc.contains("\tnil\n") : sites ||: else : sites.append(sacc)
            pj => pj + 1
            self :> xe

    pass <: od -> pass
        |: sret == "e"
        then:
            sacc => sacc + ((self.sx_text(gi + 2) + "\t") + (od_tk + "\n"))
            gi => self.sx_next(gi)
            self :> xy

    # The reduce. A stream's first site sets its C types, a later one must
    # agree key by key.
    pass <: xr -> pass
        |: qk < sites.count() and not self.has_key(stab, s_stream)
        then:
            sacc => s_args
            sprev => ""
            srow => ""
            self :> xk

    pass <: xr -> pass
        |: qk < sites.count() and self.has_key(stab, s_stream)
        then:
            sacc => s_args
            sprev => self.look(stab, s_stream)
            self :> xm

    pass <: xr -> pass
        |: qk >= sites.count()
        then:
            pk => pk + 1
            self :> xa

    pass <: xk -> pass
        |: sacc != "" and not self.iserr(sa_ct)
        then:
            srow => srow + ((" (" + sa_k) + ((" " + self.pr(sa_tk)) + ((" \"" + sa_ct) + "\")")))
            sprev => sprev + (sa_tk + self.soh)
            sacc => self.cut(sacc, sa_line.length() + 1)
            self :> xk

    pass <: xk -> done
        |: sacc != "" and self.iserr(sa_ct)
        then:
            out => epre + ("\nerror|" + self.cut(sa_ct, 3))

    pass <: xk -> pass
        |: sacc == ""
        then:
            stab => self.put_last(stab, s_stream, sprev)
            orows => orows.append((("(spi " + owner) + (" " + s_stream)) + (srow + ")"))
            qk => qk + 1
            self :> xr

    pass <: xm -> pass
        |: sacc != "" and self.pr(sa_tk) == self.pr(sp_tk)
        then:
            sacc => self.cut(sacc, sa_line.length() + 1)
            sprev => self.cut(sprev, sp_tk.length() + 1)
            self :> xm

    pass <: xm -> done
        |: sacc != "" and self.pr(sa_tk) != self.pr(sp_tk)
        then:
            out => epre + ("\nerror|" + self.cut(m_incon, 3))

    pass <: xm -> pass
        |: sacc == ""
        then:
            qk => qk + 1
            self :> xr

    # The typer. `go` types the node at `cur`, `rt` hands `val` to the
    # frame on top, and the run ends back in the pass with `od`.
    ty <: go -> ty
        |: iv != ""
        then:
            val => iv
            self :> rt

    ty <: go -> ty
        |: iv == "" and gh == "binop"
        then:
            fr => fr.slice(0, fd).append(Frame(n: cur, st: 1, a: "", b: -1, c: ""))
            fd => fd + 1
            cur => cur + 3
            self :> go

    ty <: go -> ty
        |: iv == "" and (gh == "neg" or gh == "not" or gh == "subscript")
        then:
            fr => fr.slice(0, fd).append(Frame(n: cur, st: 3, a: "", b: -1, c: ""))
            fd => fd + 1
            cur => cur + 2
            self :> go

    ty <: go -> ty
        |: iv == "" and gh == "dot"
        then:
            fr => fr.slice(0, fd).append(Frame(n: cur, st: 4, a: "", b: -1, c: ""))
            fd => fd + 1
            cur => cur + 2
            self :> go

    ty <: go -> ty
        |: iv == "" and gh == "multi-arm"
        then:
            cur => self.sx_next(cur + 4)
            self :> go

    ty <: go -> ty
        |: iv == "" and gh == "chained-cmp"
        then:
            fr => fr.slice(0, fd).append(Frame(n: cur, st: 6, a: "0", b: self.sx_next(cur + 2), c: ""))
            fd => fd + 1
            cur => self.sx_next(cur + 2)
            self :> go

    ty <: go -> ty
        |: iv == "" and gh == "do"
        then:
            fr => fr.slice(0, fd).append(Frame(n: cur, st: 7, a: "-1", b: cur + 2, c: ctx_save))
            fd => fd + 1
            self :> ds

    ty <: go -> ty
        |: iv == "" and gh == "call" and ch == "dot"
        then:
            fr => fr.slice(0, fd).append(Frame(n: cur, st: 5, a: "", b: -1, c: ""))
            fd => fd + 1
            cur => cc + 2
            self :> go

    # A TF signature's return type, after the comma at depth zero.
    ty <: go -> ty
        |: iv == "" and gh == "call" and ch == "foreign-ref"
        then:
            tfs => c_sig
            tfp => 3
            tfd => 0
            self :> tf

    ty <: go -> ty
        |: iv == "" and (gh == "foreign-selector-call" or gh == "foreign-class-selector-call") and self.sx_text(cur + 5).starts_with("TF(")
        then:
            tfs => self.sx_text(cur + 5)
            tfp => 3
            tfd => 0
            self :> tf

    ty <: go -> ty
        |: iv == "" and (gh == "foreign-selector-call" or gh == "foreign-class-selector-call") and not self.sx_text(cur + 5).starts_with("TF(")
        then:
            val => self.m_nyi("FL-3: unknown foreign type-node kind ")
            self :> rt

    # clamp and stackalloc count their args first.
    ty <: go -> ty
        |: is_cid and nac < 0
        then:
            nac => 0
            aci => c_a1
            self :> ac

    ty <: go -> ty
        |: is_cid and nac >= 0 and cnm == "stackalloc"
        then:
            val => iv_sa
            nac => -1
            self :> rt

    ty <: go -> ty
        |: is_cid and nac >= 0 and cnm == "clamp" and nac != 3
        then:
            val => self.m_user("clamp expects 3 args (x, lo, hi), got " + nac.to_string())
            nac => -1
            self :> rt

    ty <: go -> ty
        |: is_cid and nac == 3 and cnm == "clamp"
        then:
            fr => fr.slice(0, fd).append(Frame(n: cur, st: 10, a: "", b: -1, c: ""))
            fd => fd + 1
            nac => -1
            cur => self.argv(c_a1)
            self :> go

    ty <: ac -> ty
        |: aci < self.sx_end(cur)
        then:
            nac => nac + 1
            aci => self.sx_next(aci)
            self :> ac

    ty <: ac -> ty
        |: aci >= self.sx_end(cur)
        then: self :> go

    ty <: tf -> ty
        |: tf_c == 44 and tfd == 0
        then:
            val => self.fty(tf_ret)
            self :> rt

    ty <: tf -> ty
        |: tf_c < 0
        then:
            val => self.m_nyi("FL-3: unknown foreign type-node kind ")
            self :> rt

    ty <: tf -> ty
        |: tf_c >= 0 and (tf_c != 44 or tfd != 0)
        then:
            tfd => ||: tf_c == 40 : tfd + 1 ||: tf_c == 41 : tfd - 1 ||: else : tfd
            tfp => tfp + 1
            self :> tf

    # A return. An error or the last frame ends the run.
    ty <: rt -> pass
        |: self.iserr(val) or fd == 0
        then:
            terr => ||: self.iserr(val) : val ||: else : ""
            fd => 0
            self :> od

    ty <: rt -> ty
        |: not self.iserr(val) and fd > 0 and ftop.st == 1
        then:
            fr => fr.slice(0, fd - 1).append(Frame(n: t_n, st: 2, a: val, b: -1, c: ""))
            cur => self.sx_next(t_n + 3)
            self :> go

    ty <: rt -> ty
        |: not self.iserr(val) and fd > 0 and ftop.st == 2
        then:
            val => self.b_res(self.sx_text(t_n + 2), ftop.a, val)
            fd => fd - 1
            self :> rt

    ty <: rt -> ty
        |: not self.iserr(val) and fd > 0 and ftop.st == 3
        then:
            val => un_res
            fd => fd - 1
            self :> rt

    ty <: rt -> ty
        |: not self.iserr(val) and fd > 0 and ftop.st == 4 and not d_res.starts_with("@")
        then:
            val => d_res
            fd => fd - 1
            self :> rt

    # A peer atom's observable, typed against its own fields with `self`
    # rebound and the locals kept.
    ty <: rt -> ty
        |: not self.iserr(val) and fd > 0 and ftop.st == 4 and d_res.starts_with("@") and fd < 60
        then:
            fr => fr.slice(0, fd - 1).append(Frame(n: t_n, st: 9, a: d_res.substring(1, 1), b: -1, c: ctx_save))
            sfk => "P"
            sfo => self.peer_a(d_res)
            loc => self.put_last(loc, "self", self.q_atom(self.peer_a(d_res)))
            cur => self.peer_e(d_res)
            self :> go

    ty <: rt -> ty
        |: not self.iserr(val) and fd > 0 and ftop.st == 4 and d_res.starts_with("@") and fd >= 60
        then:
            val => "!N:port: out of scope"
            self :> rt

    ty <: rt -> ty
        |: not self.iserr(val) and fd > 0 and ftop.st == 5
        then:
            val => m_res
            fd => fd - 1
            self :> rt

    ty <: rt -> ty
        |: not self.iserr(val) and fd > 0 and ftop.st == 6 and ch_next < self.sx_end(t_n)
        then:
            fr => fr.slice(0, fd - 1).append(Frame(n: t_n, st: 6, a: ch_a, b: ch_next, c: ""))
            cur => ch_next
            self :> go

    ty <: rt -> ty
        |: not self.iserr(val) and fd > 0 and ftop.st == 6 and ch_next >= self.sx_end(t_n)
        then:
            val => self.wrapif(ch_flag, ":bool")
            fd => fd - 1
            self :> rt

    ty <: rt -> ty
        |: not self.iserr(val) and fd > 0 and (ftop.st == 8 or ftop.st == 9)
        then:
            val => ||: ftop.st == 9 and ftop.a == "O" : self.wrapopt(self.unw(val)) ||: else : val
            sfk => self.c_sfk(ftop.c)
            sfo => self.c_sfo(ftop.c)
            loc => self.c_loc(ftop.c)
            fd => fd - 1
            self :> rt

    ty <: rt -> ty
        |: not self.iserr(val) and fd > 0 and ftop.st == 10
        then:
            val => ||: self.num(val) : val ||: else : self.m_user("clamp arg must be numeric; got " + self.pr(val))
            fd => fd - 1
            self :> rt

    ty <: rt -> ty
        |: not self.iserr(val) and fd > 0 and ftop.st == 11
        then:
            loc => self.put_last(loc, self.sx_text(ds_k + 2), val)
            fr => fr.slice(0, fd - 1).append(Frame(n: t_n, st: 7, a: ds_k.to_string(), b: self.sx_next(ds_k), c: ftop.c))
            self :> ds

    # The do-block. Each `let` and `alias` binds a local in turn, then the
    # last statement is the value when it is an expression statement.
    ty <: ds -> ty
        |: not ds_done and ds_h == "let" and ds_ty != "nil" and self.iserr(ds_ann)
        then:
            val => ds_ann
            self :> rt

    ty <: ds -> ty
        |: not ds_done and ds_h == "let" and ds_ty != "nil" and not self.iserr(ds_ann)
        then:
            loc => self.put_last(loc, self.sx_text(ds_k + 2), ds_ann)
            fr => fr.slice(0, fd - 1).append(Frame(n: t_n, st: 7, a: ds_k.to_string(), b: self.sx_next(ds_k), c: ftop.c))
            self :> ds

    ty <: ds -> ty
        |: not ds_done and ds_eval
        then:
            fr => fr.slice(0, fd - 1).append(Frame(n: t_n, st: 11, a: ds_k.to_string(), b: ds_k, c: ftop.c))
            cur => ds_expr
            self :> go

    ty <: ds -> ty
        |: not ds_done and ds_h != "alias" and ds_h != "let"
        then:
            fr => fr.slice(0, fd - 1).append(Frame(n: t_n, st: 7, a: ds_k.to_string(), b: self.sx_next(ds_k), c: ftop.c))
            self :> ds

    ty <: ds -> ty
        |: ds_done and ds_last >= 0 and self.sx_head(ds_last) == "expr-stmt"
        then:
            fr => fr.slice(0, fd - 1).append(Frame(n: t_n, st: 8, a: "", b: -1, c: ftop.c))
            cur => ds_last + 2
            self :> go

    ty <: ds -> ty
        |: ds_done and (ds_last < 0 or self.sx_head(ds_last) != "expr-stmt")
        then:
            val => ":void"
            sfk => self.c_sfk(ftop.c)
            sfo => self.c_sfo(ftop.c)
            loc => self.c_loc(ftop.c)
            fd => fd - 1
            self :> rt

    # Selection sort over `rows` into `sorted`, keeping repeats, then back
    # to the pass named by `sort_ret`.
    sorting <: scan -> sorting
        |: sort_i < rows.count() and not scan_has
        then:
            scan_best => scan_cur
            scan_has => true
            sort_i => sort_i + 1
            self :> scan

    sorting <: scan -> sorting
        |: sort_i < rows.count() and scan_has and scan_cmp < 0
        then:
            scan_best => scan_cur
            sort_i => sort_i + 1
            self :> scan

    sorting <: scan -> sorting
        |: sort_i < rows.count() and scan_has and scan_cmp >= 0
        then:
            sort_i => sort_i + 1
            self :> scan

    sorting <: scan -> sorting
        |: sort_i >= rows.count() and scan_has
        then:
            sorted => sorted + ("\n" + scan_best).repeat(s_cnt)
            nsorted => nsorted + s_cnt
            rows => s_left
            sort_i => 0
            scan_has => false
            scan_best => ""
            self :> scan

    sorting <: scan -> pass
        |: s_done and sort_ret == "hint"
        then:
            rhint => self.put_last(rhint, owner, self.cut(sorted, 1).replace("\n", ", "))
            sorted => ""
            nsorted => 0
            pk => pk + 1
            self :> ow

    sorting <: scan -> pass
        |: s_done and sort_ret == "R"
        then:
            rsec => rsec + ((("\n(record-obs " + nsorted.to_string()) + ")") + sorted)
            rotab => ||: rnd == 2 : rotab2 ||: else : rotab
            sorted => ""
            nsorted => 0
            pass => "A"
            pk => 0
            self :> ow

    sorting <: scan -> pass
        |: s_done and sort_ret == "A"
        then:
            rsec => rsec + ((("\n(atom-obs " + nsorted.to_string()) + ")") + sorted)
            aobs => ||: rnd == 2 : aobs2 ||: else : aobs
            sorted => ""
            nsorted => 0
            pass => "S"
            pk => 0
            self :> xa

    sorting <: scan -> done
        |: s_done and sort_ret == "S" and (mode != "round2" or rnd == 2)
        then:
            out => rsec + ((("\n(stream-payloads " + nsorted.to_string()) + ")") + sorted)

    # (round2) The first round is done, the protocol defaults are next.
    sorting <: scan -> pass
        |: s_done and sort_ret == "S" and mode == "round2" and rnd == 1
        then:
            sorted => ""
            nsorted => 0
            rsec => ""
            self :> pd0

    sorting <: scan -> done
        |: s_done and sort_ret == "D" and p_err
        then:
            out => ((("\n(protocol-defaults " + nsorted.to_string()) + ")") + sorted) + ("\n" + p_errl)

    sorting <: scan -> pass
        |: s_done and sort_ret == "D" and not p_err
        then:
            rsec => (("\n(protocol-defaults " + nsorted.to_string()) + ")") + sorted
            sorted => ""
            nsorted => 0
            rnd => 2
            pass => "R"
            pk => 0
            self :> ow

    sorting <: scan -> done
        |: s_done and sort_ret == "H"
        then:
            out => fpre + (("\nerror|" + hx_base) + hx_list)
